Now we substitute $\blueD{g(x)=x^5-2x}$ and $\goldD{g'(x)=5x^4-2}$ into the equation:

$\begin{align}
\goldD{g'(x)}&=\dfrac{2x+5\blueD{g(x)}}{x}
\\\\
\goldD{5x^4-2}&\stackrel{?}{=}\dfrac{2x+5\left(\blueD{x^5-2x}\right)}{x}
\\\\
5x^4-2&\stackrel{?}{=}\dfrac{2x+5x^5-10x}{x}
\\\\
5x^4-2&\stackrel{?}{=}\dfrac{5x^5-8x}{x}
\\\\
5x^4-2&\stackrel{?}{=} 5x^4-8
\\\\
-2&\neq -8
\end{align}$

We did not obtain equivalent expressions on each side.
